>>>malloy
source: chem_quantity_loss is duckdb.table('./chem-quantity-lost.csv')
    extend {
    measure:
    total_milliliters_lost is sum(milliliter)
    total_units_lost is sum(unit)
    combined_loss is sum(milliliter) + sum(unit)
    total_states is count(state)

    view: by_state is {
    group_by: 
        state
    aggregate: combined_loss
   }

   # shape_map
   view: by_state_shaped is by_state

    }
>>>markdown
**(1)** This dataset includes data from the years 2019, 2020, 2021, and 2022. However, the data for 2022 is only partially included, covering the months from January through September. 
>>>malloy
run: chem_quantity_loss -> {
    aggregate: 
        StartDate is min(period)
        EndDate is max(period)
}
>>>markdown
**(2)** The dataset contains records from 45 U.S. statesm providing broad geographic coverage across the country.
>>>malloy
run: chem_quantity_loss -> {
    aggregate: total_states
}
>>>markdown
**(3)** The following code displays the total amount of controled substance loss reported by each state included in the dataset.
>>>malloy
run: chem_quantity_loss -> {
    group_by: state
    aggregate: combined_loss
    order_by: combined_loss desc

}
>>>markdown
**(4)** The following code generates a heat map highlighting the U.S. states affected by controlled substance loss. The color intensity corresponds to the severity of the loss, with darker shades indicating higher total losses.
>>>malloy
run: chem_quantity_loss->by_state_shaped
>>>markdown
**(5)** The below code produces a bar chart grouped by reporting period, showing the total combined loss of controlled substances for each period. 
>>>malloy
# bar_chart
run: chem_quantity_loss -> {
    group_by: period
    aggregate: combined_loss
    order_by: period desc
}
>>>markdown
**(6)** The following code displays a breakdown of total milliliters lost, total units lost, and the total combined loss amount. It is grouped by each type of loss reported in the dataset.
>>>malloy
run: chem_quantity_loss -> {
  group_by: loss_type
  aggregate: total_milliliters_lost
  aggregate: total_units_lost
  aggregate: combined_loss
  order_by: total_units_lost desc  
}
>>>markdown
**(7)** The following code displays a breakdown of total milliliters lost, total units lost, and the total combined loss amount. It is grouped by each type of business activity reported in the dataset.
>>>malloy
run: chem_quantity_loss -> {
    group_by: business_activity
    aggregate: total_milliliters_lost
    aggregate: total_units_lost
    aggregate: combined_loss
    order_by: total_units_lost desc  
}